# rapid-horizons on the Horizons spawn (the CottageCore Lobby, rapidskies:spawn; rapid-core
# profile next door). Positions come from the build itself; fine-tune in-game with
# /horizons here (prints copyable lines) and /horizons reload, then put the final values
# here, or the next `rsdeploy.py apply` puts these back.

# The way into the Heartland: an arch across the gravel path that leaves the round plaza to
# the south, 12 blocks behind the spawn and facing it, between the path's mossy cobblestone
# curbs (x -3 and 3). The opening is the path's full width (x -2..2), standing height y 72
# (the path's top) to 76, one block thick at z 12. rapid-horizons builds the arch around it
# (rtp.portal.build); the north, east and west roads off the plaza stay clear.
rtp.portal.region: "rapidskies:spawn, -2, 72, 12, 2, 76, 12"
rtp.portal.build: true
# "The Heartland" floating in front of the arch: centred on the opening (x 0.5), a block and a
# half out on the plaza side (z 10.5), its bottom at y 75 so it clears the heads of players
# walking up the path and reads at eye level from the plaza.
rtp.portal.hologram: "rapidskies:spawn, 0.5, 75, 10.5"

# NPCs on the plaza's four raised pedestals (double slabs at y 73, on the diagonals 5.7
# blocks from the spawn), each facing the centrepiece; they turn to look at players nearby.
# Players spawn facing north, so the two in front come first: the Heartland Guide on the
# right, the Land Surveyor (/claim help) on the left. Behind: the Trade Master on the right,
# by the path to the arch, and the way back to the lobby on the left.
npcs.heartland.location: "rapidskies:spawn, 4.5, 74, -3.5, 45, 0"
npcs.land.location: "rapidskies:spawn, -3.5, 74, -3.5, -45, 0"
npcs.trades.location: "rapidskies:spawn, 4.5, 74, 4.5, 135, 0"
npcs.hub.location: "rapidskies:spawn, -3.5, 74, 4.5, -135, 0"

# All four Frontier modifiers in the rotation, the launch two first so a running rotation
# carries on where it was (a live config written before Shattered Skies and Deep Dark lists
# only those two, and new keys don't replace existing ones).
frontier.modifiers: [overgrowth, drought, shattered-skies, deep-dark]
